		+ internalEffectContainer:count()
		+ internalPartContainer:count()
		+ internalSoundContainer:count()


	local success, result = pcall(fs.read, fs, "autoload.txt")

	-- Autoload runs inside init(), which is part of the synchronous boot chain BEFORE the menu
	-- window is built (Luma.init -> SaveManager.init -> ... -> Menu.init). If the autoload target
	-- has since been deleted, SaveManager.load would hit its read-failure branch and fire a
	-- Library:Notify before the notification UI exists -- that error would bubble out of init and
	-- stop the whole menu from loading. So: only attempt the autoload if the referenced config
	-- file still exists, and pcall the load so a missing/corrupt config can never abort boot.
